WEBVTT

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:32.740
Hey, Yujin.

00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:37.320
I like how that name sounds.

00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:41.240
I'm sure your fiancé likes it too.

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:44.210
How pretty.

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:47.290
Your ring, I mean.

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:54.670
It's really pretty, but it doesn't look very good on you.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:56.300
That's an engagement ring, I assume?

00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:59.980
They say that the face of a woman in love is...

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:01.350
How should I say it?

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:04.180
They say it sparkles.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:06.690
But yours sure doesn't seem like it.

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:09.730
Maybe it's because you two have been seeing each other for so long.

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:14.690
I see you have a variety of interests, Director.

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:18.070
I just want to know what kind of a person you are, Miss Yujin.

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:20.370
Oh I know, you've got the marriage blues, don't you?

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:24.700
They say that women get depressed just before they get married, right?

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:27.410
"Is he really Mr. Right?"

00:01:27.410 --> 00:01:29.130
"Should I really marry him?"

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:32.920
You even start losing your confidence.

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:35.090
I think that's enough.

00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:40.870
I honestly find it unpleasant that you're talking about me

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:42.700
as if you know me well.

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:44.600
I must be right, then.

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:47.810
You'd have no reason to be unpleasant if I was totally off the mark.

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:49.270
Director.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:51.960
My name is Minhyung Lee.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:53.730
The least you could do is call me by name.

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:35.470
He's at the ski resort.

00:03:35.470 --> 00:03:38.300
He canceled all his other appointments for the day and left.

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:39.300
Really?

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:41.470
Thank you.

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:44.300
Miss Chelin?

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:45.340
What brings you to the office?

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:47.260
Deputy Manager Kim.

00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:50.640
I stopped by, thinking I'd have some tea with him.

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:53.940
I came to the office since he wasn't picking up his cell phone.

00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:56.480
Maybe he forgot to take it with him.

00:03:56.610 --> 00:03:58.780
More importantly, I think you've gotten even prettier than before.

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:00.610
You think so?

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:03.860
Minhyung must be treating you well.

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:06.660
Why did he go to the ski resort?

00:04:07.070 --> 00:04:08.740
He didn't tell <i>me</i> about it.

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:11.450
I was actually supposed to go,

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:13.650
but he said there was something in the contract he had to approve himself,

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:15.040
so he went instead.

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:16.540
I see.

00:04:17.710 --> 00:04:18.840
Not to mention,

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:20.150
he went alone with the beautiful woman

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:21.300
from the company we're working with.

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:24.470
Oh, really?

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:26.810
Aren't you worried?

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:28.800
He's alone with another woman.

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:31.930
I think we're already past that stage.

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:34.190
He should be back by the end of the day, right?

00:04:34.390 --> 00:04:37.520
I certainly hope so.

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:40.900
I hope he comes back today so you won't have to keep worrying...

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:43.640
Oh, don't tease me like that.

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:46.910
It's not like I don't get enough of that from Minhyung already.

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:49.780
I was about to leave for the ski resort too,

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:52.620
so I'll make it my mission to bring him back to you by the end of the day.

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:54.180
Okay.

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:55.870
Excuse me for one moment.

00:04:56.710 --> 00:04:58.330
Hyeoksoo Kim speaking.

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:00.370
Oh hello, Miss Jeong-a.

00:05:00.370 --> 00:05:02.210
I heard something happened; is everything all right?

00:05:03.590 --> 00:05:05.720
Yes, the director went in my stead.

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:07.760
The ski resort called us not too long ago.

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:09.550
They said he arrived safely with Miss Yujin.

00:05:10.430 --> 00:05:11.850
Oh no, I'm about to leave myself.

00:05:12.270 --> 00:05:14.430
<i>I'm planning on helping out at the ski resort too.</i>

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:18.770
<i>We'll all have to make sacrifices if we want this to work, right?</i>

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:24.400
Could I see the wiring diagram for the annex building?

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:26.000
Sure thing.

00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:28.700
Could you go get the wiring diagram, Choi?

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:34.660
Here's the wiring diagram you asked for.

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:37.000
Yes, thank you.

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:43.460
<i>Oh, Miss Yujin from Polaris?</i>

00:05:43.590 --> 00:05:45.450
<i>She's an employee at the company we're working with.</i>

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:46.050
<i>Why?</i>

00:06:05.610 --> 00:06:06.780
It's cold, isn't it?

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:08.280
I'm fine.

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:09.610
No, you're not;

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:11.570
your lips are all blue.

00:06:12.910 --> 00:06:13.580
But...

00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:15.870
We've got work to do here.

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:18.150
Even if you catch a cold, I'm not going to let you off the hook,

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:19.580
so take care of yourself.

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:24.090
Sorry if it smells a little; it's been in the trunk for a while.

00:06:45.980 --> 00:06:48.610
How much progress have we made on the construction?

00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:51.790
The report said we shouldn't have any problems getting things ready

00:06:51.790 --> 00:06:53.070
before the opening date.

00:06:57.240 --> 00:06:59.410
This road leads to the old building, doesn't it?

00:07:17.310 --> 00:07:18.310
They're kissing.

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:20.020
Hey, Yujin.

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:29.400
This is much better than I expected.

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:37.580
I didn't think you would come here yourself, Director.

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:52.650
Hi, this is Program Director Kim speaking.

00:08:53.320 --> 00:08:56.820
I'm calling you about the Christmas Special; it's going to be a live event.

00:08:57.200 --> 00:08:57.880
Yes.

00:08:58.660 --> 00:09:01.490
I was wondering if you could look up a few venues for me.

00:09:01.870 --> 00:09:04.870
Preferably an outdoor one, since it's going to be a Christmas concert.

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:05.580
Yes.

00:09:07.020 --> 00:09:07.500
Yes.

00:09:07.830 --> 00:09:09.840
Please check those for me and then call me back.

00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:32.940
Hi, Sanghyuk.

00:09:33.070 --> 00:09:33.900
<i>Where are you?</i>

00:09:34.530 --> 00:09:35.930
I'm at the ski resort;

00:09:35.930 --> 00:09:37.570
I had to check up on a few things here.

00:09:38.030 --> 00:09:39.360
<i>You didn't tell me you were going.</i>

00:09:39.570 --> 00:09:40.950
It just happened.

00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:44.830
<i>I wanted to have dinner with you, but I guess we can't, huh?</i>

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:46.470
Doesn't look like it.

00:09:46.470 --> 00:09:48.920
I'll call you when I'm back in Seoul though.

00:09:50.920 --> 00:09:51.920
Your fiancé?

00:09:52.840 --> 00:09:54.360
I didn't mean to eavesdrop.

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:55.210
Shall we go?

00:09:57.510 --> 00:09:58.640
We need to look at the other side of the resort too.

00:09:58.640 --> 00:09:59.550
Hurry up.

00:10:12.770 --> 00:10:14.360
What brings you here?

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:16.720
I figured I'd drop by,

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:18.560
since I'm helping out with the costumes for one of the programs here.

00:10:18.560 --> 00:10:19.530
You're doing well, I hope?

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:20.360
Of course.

00:10:20.360 --> 00:10:22.700
How are things going at the store?

00:10:22.830 --> 00:10:23.580
Not bad.

00:10:26.870 --> 00:10:28.940
How is Yujin these days?

00:10:28.940 --> 00:10:30.460
Has she said anything strange lately?

00:10:31.290 --> 00:10:32.080
About what?

00:10:34.210 --> 00:10:36.960
About Minhyung, for example.

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:39.550
Oh, you mean the guy you brought over?

00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:41.890
Are you all right?

00:10:42.220 --> 00:10:43.680
Of course, why wouldn't I be?

00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:46.810
I was surprised at first, but he's <i>your</i> boyfriend, right?

00:10:47.600 --> 00:10:48.850
I'll just have to get used to it.

00:10:54.820 --> 00:10:55.740
Oh yeah,

00:10:55.740 --> 00:10:59.570
Yujin was put in charge of renovating a ski resort this time around.

00:10:59.990 --> 00:11:01.620
She's over there right now.

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:04.010
She seems really eager about the project;

00:11:04.010 --> 00:11:05.450
it's something she's always wanted to do.

00:11:05.740 --> 00:11:06.840
Thank goodness.

00:11:06.840 --> 00:11:09.370
I was worried that you'd be uncomfortable with it.

00:11:09.830 --> 00:11:10.620
With what?

00:11:10.960 --> 00:11:13.780
Minhyung couldn't stop raving about Yujin.

00:11:13.780 --> 00:11:15.880
He said she's very diligent and dedicated to her work.

00:11:16.670 --> 00:11:17.670
What are you talking about?

00:11:17.670 --> 00:11:18.920
Why would he rave about her?

00:11:19.170 --> 00:11:22.430
Minhyung is actually the one overseeing the ski resort construction.

00:11:24.930 --> 00:11:26.390
I thought you knew about it.

00:11:27.260 --> 00:11:29.120
Why don't we go there together right now?

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:30.430
I was going to go see Minhyung anyway.

00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:32.440
I already called Yongguk and Jinsook.

00:11:32.810 --> 00:11:36.150
Did Yujin really not say anything about it?

00:11:37.900 --> 00:11:39.940
Maybe I shouldn't have mentioned it...

00:11:40.400 --> 00:11:43.280
Oh no, I've just been busy these days, that's all.

00:11:44.660 --> 00:11:45.620
I see.

00:11:45.620 --> 00:11:46.700
Why don't we get going then?

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:51.910
What kind of a house do you want to live in after you get married?

00:11:52.410 --> 00:11:54.670
I've never really thought about it.

00:11:55.830 --> 00:11:56.560
Really?

00:11:56.560 --> 00:11:58.180
So you've never thought about

00:11:58.180 --> 00:11:59.840
the house you'd want to share with the love of your life -

00:11:59.960 --> 00:12:01.520
like what kind of a hallway it should have,

00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:02.970
or how the bedroom should look -

00:12:03.090 --> 00:12:04.930
you've really never thought about these things at all?

00:12:05.260 --> 00:12:07.930
I think those kind of things

00:12:07.930 --> 00:12:10.020
aren't important if you really love each other.

00:12:10.350 --> 00:12:10.970
Then...

00:12:12.270 --> 00:12:14.980
I don't think the physical form of a house is all that important.

00:12:16.940 --> 00:12:21.940
After all, a loving heart is the best house any loving couple could ask for.

00:12:37.670 --> 00:12:39.500
Stop it, you're going to flood the car with your tears.

00:12:40.460 --> 00:12:42.010
Would you stop crying?

00:12:42.130 --> 00:12:44.550
I bet you'd be crying too right now, if you were me.

00:12:44.670 --> 00:12:45.430
Here.

00:12:50.390 --> 00:12:53.520
I can't say anything about their age restriction, but height and weight?

00:12:54.390 --> 00:12:55.430
Do you have to be a supermodel

00:12:55.430 --> 00:12:57.020
to work at a pharmaceutical company these days?

00:12:58.400 --> 00:13:00.400
If you're not going to be employed for the time being,

00:13:01.230 --> 00:13:04.400
why don't you take that real estate exam you were studying for again?

00:13:05.780 --> 00:13:08.280
You think <i>I</i> would be able to pass a test like that?

00:13:08.740 --> 00:13:12.910
You know I'm no good at taking tests.

00:13:13.080 --> 00:13:15.910
I just can't pass no matter how hard I try.

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:19.840
Say something, will you?

00:13:19.960 --> 00:13:22.960
This world will one day see you for who you are, Jinsook.

00:13:23.510 --> 00:13:24.510
You think so?

00:13:24.840 --> 00:13:25.970
Either way, quit sobbing.

00:13:26.090 --> 00:13:27.900
We're here for a change of air, aren't we?

00:13:27.900 --> 00:13:31.260
Let's have fun at the ski resort and forget all about it, okay?

00:13:50.030 --> 00:13:51.120
What are you doing?

00:13:51.280 --> 00:13:52.620
Stepping in your footprints.

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:54.870
This way I can remember you.

00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:17.140
I heard there was an open area we could use to hold events.

00:14:17.550 --> 00:14:18.750
Ah, yes.

00:14:27.780 --> 00:14:30.160
That guy... Minhyung I mean.

00:14:31.700 --> 00:14:33.410
How did you meet him?

00:14:35.160 --> 00:14:36.410
So you're curious too?

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:38.910
I'm just asking.

00:14:39.410 --> 00:14:42.580
I just figured we have a lot of time to talk before we get to the resort.

00:14:42.830 --> 00:14:44.000
How did you two meet?

00:14:44.170 --> 00:14:45.500
Why is that important?

00:14:48.340 --> 00:14:51.890
What's important is that we love each other.

00:14:53.640 --> 00:14:55.390
You don't mind if I turn the radio up, do you?

00:14:55.510 --> 00:14:58.170
<i>It looks like everyone driving through this region</i>

00:14:58.170 --> 00:15:01.140
<i>will need to pay special attention;</i>

00:15:01.350 --> 00:15:04.670
<i>especially if you're driving through the Kangwon mountain area,</i>

00:15:04.670 --> 00:15:06.340
<i>where snowstorm alerts have been issued.</i>

00:15:09.780 --> 00:15:13.530
The facility itself has gotten quite creaky,

00:15:13.660 --> 00:15:15.140
so we intend to replace the gondola lifts

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:17.080
during the renovation process as well.

00:15:18.240 --> 00:15:22.210
So all that's left now is to visit the restaurant and the café, correct?

00:15:22.460 --> 00:15:25.710
Yes, that's all we have on the schedule for now.

00:15:26.130 --> 00:15:28.050
Why don't we go on ahead, Miss Yujin.

00:15:41.390 --> 00:15:42.310
Miss Yujin?

00:15:44.350 --> 00:15:47.400
You're a woman of few words, aren't you?

00:15:47.770 --> 00:15:50.400
It's the first time a woman hasn't shown much interest in me.

00:15:51.990 --> 00:15:53.860
It's a little hard to adapt to, to be honest.

00:15:55.240 --> 00:15:56.700
I've got nothing to say to that.

00:15:57.450 --> 00:15:58.580
I'm just joking.

00:16:00.290 --> 00:16:03.830
Now I'm embarrassed that you took it seriously.

00:16:08.380 --> 00:16:09.550
What do you think?

00:16:10.090 --> 00:16:12.390
I can't say anything about the interior at this moment,

00:16:12.390 --> 00:16:14.510
but Polaris' current plan is to replace the windows and varnish inside,

00:16:14.630 --> 00:16:18.470
while leaving the basic building frame intact.

00:16:29.610 --> 00:16:30.320
Please.

00:16:40.790 --> 00:16:43.540
I want to make it look brick-like.

00:16:44.460 --> 00:16:45.960
Aren't there too many columns here?

00:16:46.620 --> 00:16:48.200
In my opinion,

00:16:48.200 --> 00:16:51.090
too many columns reduce the amount of space available for use.

00:16:52.420 --> 00:16:55.590
I think if we could somehow place the tables effectively,

00:16:55.720 --> 00:16:58.600
it'd actually help to offer a sense of privacy.

00:16:59.220 --> 00:16:59.890
Excuse me?

00:17:00.350 --> 00:17:03.470
Whether they're families or lovers,

00:17:03.600 --> 00:17:06.270
the time they spend here should be special, right?

00:17:06.770 --> 00:17:08.480
I think if we can use the columns well,

00:17:09.190 --> 00:17:13.740
they'll be able to separate the areas, creating a sense of coziness.

00:17:14.570 --> 00:17:16.820
I guess they could.

00:17:20.490 --> 00:17:21.340
How about it?

00:17:21.340 --> 00:17:22.990
Can you imagine what it might look like?

00:17:23.330 --> 00:17:24.080
Oh...

00:17:25.830 --> 00:17:26.920
Yes.

00:17:28.290 --> 00:17:32.460
Since our overarching concept is "brown," I'll accentuate with "white."

00:17:33.840 --> 00:17:34.760
Do you like white?

00:17:37.300 --> 00:17:38.840
Do you like winter?

00:17:40.550 --> 00:17:41.680
I do.

00:17:42.140 --> 00:17:44.060
What kind of food do you like?

00:17:45.520 --> 00:17:47.230
Why do you ask?

00:17:48.690 --> 00:17:50.440
I just want to memorize what you like.

00:18:18.220 --> 00:18:19.680
Be careful and stay next to me.

00:18:34.190 --> 00:18:35.270
Wait here for a second.

00:18:59.920 --> 00:19:01.180
Maybe it's because of the weather.

00:19:01.970 --> 00:19:04.350
We'll have to stay here for the time being.

00:19:08.100 --> 00:19:09.310
Come sit here.

00:19:10.940 --> 00:19:12.400
You need to warm your body up first.

00:19:12.560 --> 00:19:14.690
Can't we just walk?

00:19:14.900 --> 00:19:16.400
We're pretty far up.

00:19:17.400 --> 00:19:20.950
Besides, walking down in this weather is a bad idea.

00:19:21.450 --> 00:19:23.780
I'm sure something will happen if we wait.

00:19:27.240 --> 00:19:30.460
There's no other way at the moment.

00:19:30.620 --> 00:19:31.870
This sure is frustrating.

00:19:32.460 --> 00:19:33.580
Deputy Manager Kim!

00:19:35.080 --> 00:19:35.590
Oh, Miss Chelin!

00:19:35.710 --> 00:19:37.880
What's going on, Deputy Manager Kim?

00:19:38.420 --> 00:19:39.810
We've got a problem.

00:19:39.810 --> 00:19:42.430
Minhyung went up to look at the restaurant,

00:19:43.130 --> 00:19:45.510
but since the gondolas can't run in this wind,

00:19:45.510 --> 00:19:46.890
he can't come back down.

00:19:47.930 --> 00:19:49.740
What can I do?

00:19:49.740 --> 00:19:51.100
There's no way down except the lifts...

00:19:51.310 --> 00:19:53.270
We've met before, haven't we?

00:19:54.480 --> 00:19:55.950
Don't worry.

00:19:55.950 --> 00:19:58.610
Miss Yujin is with our director,

00:19:59.150 --> 00:20:00.690
so there's nothing to worry about.

00:20:02.320 --> 00:20:03.110
That means...

00:20:13.330 --> 00:20:15.120
Your shoes are wet, aren't they?

00:20:16.630 --> 00:20:17.840
Why don't you dry them off here?

00:20:33.180 --> 00:20:35.480
I'll scratch your back if you scratch mine, right?

00:20:42.110 --> 00:20:44.240
You know we're supposed to broadcast together during lunch today, right?

00:21:07.010 --> 00:21:09.720
Where did you go to high school?

00:21:11.390 --> 00:21:13.160
What high school did you graduate from?

00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:14.810
Was it in America?

00:21:15.140 --> 00:21:17.730
Did you really go to high school in America?

00:21:18.900 --> 00:21:21.270
Yes, that's right.

00:21:21.400 --> 00:21:23.900
Have you heard of Chuncheon?

00:21:25.030 --> 00:21:27.950
Don't you remember Jeil High School in Chuncheon?

00:21:28.070 --> 00:21:30.700
Are you sure you've never lived in Korea before?

00:21:32.820 --> 00:21:34.470
Please, one question at a time.

00:21:34.470 --> 00:21:36.250
I'm surprised you've held back from asking for so long.

00:21:36.910 --> 00:21:39.210
Could you take off your glasses for a minute?

00:21:39.830 --> 00:21:44.050
Just this once, could you take off your glasses just for a minute?

00:21:46.340 --> 00:21:48.760
He's in no way related to Joonsang.

00:21:48.970 --> 00:21:50.800
Joonsang's dead, as you know.

00:21:57.600 --> 00:21:59.600
Miss Yujin?

00:22:00.850 --> 00:22:02.270
What should we do?

00:22:02.400 --> 00:22:03.320
I'm so worried.

00:22:03.440 --> 00:22:04.780
Minhyung...

00:22:04.900 --> 00:22:06.440
The director still isn't back?

00:22:06.610 --> 00:22:08.860
I just checked with the weather bureau,

00:22:08.990 --> 00:22:12.240
and it looks like we won't be able to run the lifts again until tomorrow.

00:22:12.580 --> 00:22:13.370
What did you say?

00:22:14.410 --> 00:22:16.790
I can't wait any longer; I'm going up there.

00:22:17.040 --> 00:22:18.580
I can't just stand around like this!

00:22:18.660 --> 00:22:19.040
Sanghyuk!

00:22:19.040 --> 00:22:20.370
Where are you going, Sanghyuk?

00:22:22.880 --> 00:22:24.000
Chelin!

00:22:30.380 --> 00:22:33.760
How are you planning on getting up there, Sanghyuk?

00:22:33.890 --> 00:22:36.140
That doesn't matter; let me go!

00:22:36.720 --> 00:22:38.770
We just have to wait until morning, right?

00:22:38.770 --> 00:22:39.770
Let's stay and wait.

00:22:40.440 --> 00:22:42.170
Wait?

00:22:42.170 --> 00:22:43.650
I can't wait any longer!

00:22:44.190 --> 00:22:45.150
Sanghyuk!

00:22:45.480 --> 00:22:46.400
I have to go!

00:22:46.400 --> 00:22:47.610
I just have to!

00:22:47.740 --> 00:22:49.320
Get a grip, man!

00:22:49.700 --> 00:22:50.570
Let me go!

00:22:50.570 --> 00:22:51.450
Let go!

00:22:57.790 --> 00:22:59.210
She'll be all right.

00:23:04.540 --> 00:23:05.420
Miss Yujin.

00:23:11.220 --> 00:23:12.010
Miss Yujin!

00:23:28.070 --> 00:23:28.860
Miss Yujin.
